hypotheses.statement:
For every fixed finite $k\geq1$, every lattice rotation or reflection of the construction, and every translate of its center to a lattice site, $$\label{sector:network-decay}
 \lim_{L\to\infty}\ \sup_{\substack{1\leq r<R\\R/r\geq L}}
 Q_k(r,R)=0.$$ This is a separately wired two-terminal network statement on the noncyclic disk sector.

Uniformly over either color and all disks in Convention <a href="#disk:conventions" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="disk:conventions">48</a>, $$\lim_{L\to\infty}
 \sup_{\substack{I\subset B(z,r),\ J\cap B(z,R)=\varnothing\\
                  R/(1+r)\ge L}}
 p(Q)=0.$$

For any fixed finite list of charges satisfying $$a_j>0,\qquad (1+a_j)\lambda<\pi/2,\qquad \sum_j a_j=1,$$ for every $\eta>0$ there is $C_{\eta,\mathbf a}<\infty$ such that the local costs obey $$\label{physical:charge-budget}
 P+D_*+\sum_j\log\frac{F_-(a_j)}{F_+(a_j)}
 \le \eta\log n+C_{\eta,\mathbf a}.$$ The assertion is valid for either global wire designation, with the fixed buffered cutoff conventions just specified.

